      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T14:43:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah true. I mentioned this because, an arbitrary big and invalid size from a misbehaving pVM can cause the host to donate lots of memory which would not be needed. Rest of the failure cases are about permissions, races and such where a huge chunk of un-necessary memory donation may not happen.",
      "parentUuid": "fc323836_f6da121c",
      "revId": "8b3efe44fbdf3bd3fb1ba56ff703e1842b66a7cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ee82a30_39c7bd2c",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 15127,
